CHANGED: Fixed two normalization slowdowns introduced by [#3250](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/pull/3250) and [#3338](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/pull/3338). The propagate-and-inline loop no longer uses `topdownFixR`, which re-descends a whole subtree every time it rewrites a node and so loses more than it saves for bundles that inline. In the cleanup phase that flattens the function hierarchy, the flattening and evaluator-backed passes are now a single bottom-up pass that runs before the top-down propagation pass, instead of two extra passes after it. Both large and small designs get faster: bittide-hardware's wireDemo drops 3.5%, and the in-repo normalization benchmarks drop 7% in total, with `T1354B.hs` 31% and `Reducer.hs` 14% faster.
